.SS "void csmp::SneddonCrackCoupled3D_VVCase::run ()\fR [virtual]\fP"
Author: E\&. Pezzulli 
.SH "Linear Elasticity: Plane stress/strain problem with central crack under uniform tension; testing the aperture profile of the crack"
.PP
Domain: "Infinite" 2D rectangle shaped model length LxL meters with central crack of half length a where L/a > 20 Mesh: Linear/Quadratic Triangles tested OK; Quadrilaterials have to be tested Material: Linear ELastic Isotropic Material: E=Young's Modulus, nu= Poisson's Ratio; Loading: No stress on boundaries\&. BC: Zero x and y displacements on LEFT BOTTOM Corner (CRN1), and zero y displacement on CRN2 (BOTTOM RIGHT) 
.SH "ConfigFiles: (\&.asc, \&.dat)"
.PP
The solution for the aperture w(x) of a horizontal fracture of half length a with origin x=0 representing middle of crack:

.PP
Plane Strain: (aperture) w = 2*Uy 4*(1 - v^2)*P/E * (a^2 - x^2 )^(1/2) E = youngs Modulus, v = Poisson Ration, a = crack half length, x = distance along crack with origin at midpoint

.PP
Marji - 2006 - Crack Tip Elements - doi:10\&.1016/j\&.ijsolstr\&.2005\&.04\&.042 Sneddon - 1946 - The opening of griffith cracks (factor of two wrong!)

.PP
The following implementation is testing the creation of the \fBFracture\fP Class, its initialisation and creation of \fBInterFace\fP Objects, constructed from opposite face pairs of the master and slave Boundaries of a 2D fracture\&. The calculation and calibration of a Unit Normal and the creation of midPoint Elements within the fracture, which are however not used/tested to work\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
The following implemetation relies on LinearElasticityIsotropicDeformation2D_VVcase to work
.RE
.PP
